**New Evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Buhari appoints Ahmed Halilu NSPMC MD","publisher":"The Nation Newspaper","publication_date":"2022-09-01","url":"https://thenationonlineng.net/buhari-appoints-ahmed-halilu-nspmc-md/","claim":"Buhari approved Ahmed Halilu as substantive managing director of the Nigerian Security Printing and Minting Company, after Halilu had served in an acting role; the report says the appointment followed a CBN governor recommendation.","locator":"lines 31-36","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous report with specific names and office, but secondary and dependent on unnamed CBN source.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about a 2022 appointment.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari because the article says he approved the appointment; the CBN recommendation limits inference about sole presidential authorship.","contrary_evidence":["Does not by itself prove nepotistic intent or personal benefit.","The report attributes the recommendation to the CBN governor and gives Halilu prior acting experience."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
- This directly strengthens the appointment-pattern gap, especially the fact of presidential approval.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Buhari appoints brother-in-law, Ahmed Halilu, to head Nigeria's currency printing company","publisher":"Ripples Nigeria","publication_date":"2022-09-01","url":"https://www.ripplesnigeria.com/buhari-appoints-brother-in-law-ahmed-halilu-to-head-nigerias-currency-printing-company/","claim":"The report says Ahmed Halilu, the elder brother to First Lady Aisha Buhari, was appointed managing director of NSPMC and that Buhari made the appointment permanent after Halilu had acted since May 16, 2022.","locator":"lines 59-60","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report with a concrete family relationship and appointment fact, though it is still secondary reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly attributable to Buhari because the article states he made the appointment permanent; family relationship supports a nepotism reading but does not prove personal gain.","contrary_evidence":["The article also notes Halilu's prior acting role and reported CBN backing, which support a competence-based explanation.","It does not show Buhari personally profited from the appointment."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
- This is the strongest direct family-appointment corroboration in the follow-up round.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"HURIWA asks Buhari to revoke Mint MD's appointment over alleged constitutional breach","publisher":"The Guardian Nigeria News","publication_date":"2022-09-02","url":"https://guardian.ng/news/huriwa-asks-buhari-to-revoke-mint-mds-appointment-over-alleged-constitutional-breach/","claim":"HURIWA publicly asked Buhari to revoke Ahmed Halilu's appointment, alleging the choice may border on nepotism and violate federal character rules because Halilu was reportedly Buhari's wife's elder brother.","locator":"lines 99-102","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_low","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting of a political/civil-society allegation, useful as contrary context but not an independent finding.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attribution is indirect: the source shows how contemporaries interpreted the appointment, not an adjudicated finding that Buhari knowingly used office for private gain.","contrary_evidence":["The article itself acknowledges Halilu's competence and professional background.","It is an allegation, not a court or audit finding."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
- This is useful contrary context, not proof of self-dealing.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Buhari Calls for Tighter Security Around Borders in Lake Chad Basin with the Proliferation of Weapons from Russia-Ukraine War","publisher":"The State House, Abuja","publication_date":"2022-11-29","url":"https://statehouse.gov.ng/president-buhari-calls-for-tighter-security-around-borders-in-lake-chad-basin-with-the-proliferation-of-weapons-from-russia-ukraine-war/","claim":"Buhari said weapons used in the Russia-Ukraine war were beginning to filter into the Lake Chad region and warned that the illegal movement of arms was heightening the proliferation of small arms and light weapons.","locator":"lines 27-33","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential press release quoting Buhari directly on the disputed claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Buhari because this is his quoted public statement, though it does not itself prove the factual claim was true.","contrary_evidence":["VOA later found the claim unsubstantiated and noted there were no public reports supporting it.","I did not locate any public correction by Buhari in the searched record."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2"]}
- This resolves the original claim side of the Ukraine-arms issue; the correction side remains weak.

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I checked targeted family-appointment coverage, official State House material, and fact-check coverage for the Lake Chad arms claim.
- I also looked for Buhari-specific asset, procurement, bribe, and audit/court findings, but the public record I found stayed at general anti-corruption context, generic asset-declaration rules, or allegations without a Buhari-specific finding.
- I rejected older or generic materials that did not add a direct personal nexus to Buhari in 2022.
- I did not retain duplicate rewrites of the same appointment story when they only repeated the same fact without adding a materially distinct claim.
- I did not find a public 2022 correction to the Lake Chad arms statement.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Personal asset/procurement/bribe/audit evidence tied directly to Buhari: `not recoverable` from the public 2022 record I searched. More search would only help if non-public filings or formal audit/court records are available.
- Family/loyalist appointment pattern: `partly resolved`. The appointment of Ahmed Halilu is now directly corroborated by both appointment and family-relationship reporting, but personal benefit or explicit Buhari knowledge beyond approval is still indirect.
- Ukraine-arms claim correction: `partly resolved`. The original statement is now directly sourced, and the existing fact-check already cuts against it, but I did not find a public correction or retraction by Buhari.

No score assigned.
